+- **2026-09-19 · Session 5 — live check, left open** · Deployed. Coaching panel made collapsible like the other sections (choice remembered). Try-that-line-again on `ma_7uk7lnh`: 139 s first try (≈90 s of it rebuilding the shed extraction, once per session per browser), **50 s steady state** — the under-a-minute half of done-when is met, with ~10 s of margin; not tuned on two data points (lever in §17). Chris's 9/18 verbal scorecard posted on 7uk7lnh in the parsed format (`scored blind`); the tab shows exact 3/6 · within-one 5/6 · same result, Evaluate AI +2 — matches the 9/18 log. · **Open: Chris scores one session blind in the new app** (he is away ~1 week). Decided with Mark: move on to session 6 and close this item when Chris is back; preferably on a fresh exam scored by `v2-rag-2`, which also gives session 6 its third scorecard. Do not rescore 7uk7lnh — it is the only session scored before Chris saw anything.
 - **2026-09-19 · Session 5 (frontend — MA History + coaching)** · Mark: happy with the MA History layout; the problem is that scores have not been consistent across the application. Diagnosis (old JSX): `summary` read in eight places — exam screen ranks attempts by sum of the legacy six, MA History shows top-level scores, Progress trends `if (scores[k])` (drops 0/missing, so averages run over different lines per session), prompts read legacy keys by name, and three different fallbacks when the JSON doesn't parse; session 3's `sectionAverages` repeated it (a legacy attempt got "TU 4.00" from one line). · Built: `src/lib/scorecard.js` — `scorecard(session,{viewer})` is the only reader: form (`2026` | `legacy`), six lines with null for missing, section averages and verdict computed from the lines (stored values ignored, mismatch → `warnings`), best-attempt rank (MA avg + TU avg; legacy never outranks 2026), mentor scorecards (structured blind items and hand-posted "… scorecard …" lines, attributed to the mentor named), per-line deltas, and the blind seal; `exam.js`, `ATExam.jsx` score screen and the legacy prompt history now go through it (no score arithmetic left elsewhere). `components/ScoreViews.jsx` (chips/grid/verdict/old-scorer tag — same view in the exam and in history). `tabs/MAHistory.jsx` (old layout; newest session open, others collapse; structured sections rendered in full with speaker colors — fixes Chris's "I only got one sentence" of peer delivery; rescore through extract → evaluate with step line, previous score kept in `score_history`, **no legacy fallback on rescore** — a failure leaves the existing score alone; draft-persisting comment box with mic; delete and rescore are candidate-only). `tabs/Rationale.jsx` (§12.2: Chris quoted inline with date, ingest-written title shown outside the quotation marks; PSIA/form citations and the level-by-level ladder collapsed). `tabs/BlindScoreForm.jsx` (§12.1: six tap rows on the 2026 form, live section averages, note, draft in localStorage, confirm, final on submit). Blind: `sealSessions()` takes the AI summary out of the session object before it reaches React state for any session the mentor hasn't scored; a sealed card carries no numbers or text; other mentors' scorecards are withheld from the thread until he submits his own; on submit the item stores `scores`, `note`, `ai_at_submit` and a text line in the same format Mark posted by hand for 7n6ry6d. **Coaching:** `lib/coaching.js` + `tabs/CoachingPanel.jsx` — per line, lowest first: what Mark said (located in the transcript, typo-tolerant), the evaluator's rewrite, the because-clause, the first Chris citation; labelled AI SUGGESTIONS; says so when the quoted line was the *peer's* (7uk7lnh Prescription), came only under examiner probing (7uk7lnh Desired Performances), or was in private notes and never spoken. **Try that line again:** `extractPassage` (same clerk, same schema, peer intent + task as reference) → `mergePassage` (items quoted from the replaced sentence out, passage items in, stats recomputed) → `assemble(original, {evidence: merged})` → `buildEvaluateLineUser` (one line, full ladder, not told the previous score) → `normalizeLine` (same clamps, citation check, equipment guard) + `unitCheck` (the evaluator's unit, checked in code against the passage alone, with the missing links named). Practice log in localStorage, last 5 per line. **Pre-exam brief** on the setup screen: three lowest lines of the last 2026-form session, ranked by Chris's scorecard when he has one. `parseAIJson` strategy 2 now rebuilds rationale for `desired_performances` and `equipment`. Summary fit: cited text 400 (Chris) / 200 (others); shed order is now justifications → extraction → citation_details, because coaching needs the extraction (7uk7lnh's was shed). `src/api.js` += `saveMaSummary`, `appendFeedback` (re-read + merge), `deleteMaSession`, `scoreLineTry`. · Verified: `npm run test:history -- <export>` (offline; also runs every row of the live MASessions export through `scorecard()`: 13 sessions → 1 on the 2026 form, 10 old-scorer, 2 unscored, 0 unparsed, 0 warnings; reproduces the 9/18 comparison exactly — exact 3/6, within-one 5/6, Evaluate +2, same result); `scripts/rendertest-history.jsx` server-renders the tab from the live export as Mark, as Chris before scoring (no AI output in any sealed session), and as Chris after submitting (reveal, per-line delta, coaching read-only); `scoreLine` run end to end with models and store mocked (query = original extraction, evidence = merged, nothing written); `vite build` clean; score/exam/zoom selftests pass. · **Not verified here (no keys, no deploy): the two model calls of try-again and its wall-clock; the blind submit against the live Sheet.** Done-when stays open until deployed: Chris scores one session blind; Mark reworks one line in under a minute. · Deferred: see §17.
 - **2026-09-19 · Session 2 (backend)** · Built: `lib/prompts/zoom.js` (`zoom-1`: mentor-only, one point per item, no generalizing, read-aloud ≠ asserted, modeled deliveries kept whole as `exemplar`, `hedged` + note, ASR fixes listed per chunk, verbatim `quote`, `tool_feedback` side channel); `lib/ingest/zoom.js` (Plaud/Zoom parser, speaker report, ~12K-char core windows with context-only padding run as parallel Opus calls, quote-in-transcript ≥60% and text-overlap ≥40% guards, dedupe, §17 `watch` marks, 409 on re-ingest unless `replacePending`); `store.js` += `insertPending` (no embedding), `listPending`, `liveStatements`, `supersessionCandidates`, `canSupersede`, `editPending`, `approveChunk` (edit → embed → approve in one update → supersede), `deletePending`, `countBySourceRef`, `deletePendingBySourceRef`; `api/ingest/zoom.js`, `api/chunks/pending.js` (GET/POST, trimmed shape, candidates per chunk), `api/chunks/approve.js` (approve / edit / delete, bulk ids); `scripts/zoom.mjs`, `scripts/selftest-zoom.mjs` (offline, passing; also run against the real 9/18 transcript: 240 turns → 3 windows of ~4.5K tok); `vercel.json` `api/ingest/*.js` 300s; `lib/http.js` `preflight` takes allowed methods. · Decided: embedding at approval, not at insert; speaker map is a prior and chunks under a non-mentor label are flagged for Chris rather than dropped (the 9/18 labels flip mid-turn: Chris appears under all three); tool feedback is not stored; approved chunks immutable; delete is a hard delete of pending only. 9/18 map from reading the transcript: Speaker 1 = chris, Speaker 2 = mark, Speaker 3 = unknown (mixed). · Deferred: see §17. · After the first live runs — `zoom-2` (standalone rule, coverage rule with ski vocabulary for ASR repair, tool feedback exclusive, progress/gear remarks excluded, fixed scores format); session-range tagging (`metadata.session_id`); two-pass union; score-line guard; `exclude` ranges. · **Done-when met 2026-09-19:** 9/18 Plaud transcript (240 turns, 1:06) ingested through the deployed endpoint — speaker map 1 = chris, 2 = mark, 3 = chris (Mark), `ma_7uk7lnh` tagged for 00:00–24:30 and 33:30–35:30 (the large-radius notes at 25:41 are a separate doc, not an MA History row — untagged), 51:24→end excluded (ski choice, per Mark). Two passes 36 + 34 → **37 pending** under `zoom:2026-09-18` (13 correction · 10 principle · 7 exemplar · 4 physics · 3 mental_model; 2 hedged, 3 check-speaker, 28 with supersession candidates), all listed by `/api/chunks/pending` with context, tags and verbatim quote; one item rejected by the score guard ("Describe 2"); stored scores chunk reads CE 2 · Ev 2 · Rx 3, matching the log. Default search returns 0 `chris_zoom`; `includeUnapproved` also 0 (no embedding). 190 s wall-clock.
